interface SavedGameState {
  round: RoundState | null;
  phase: GamePhase;
  result: GuessSubmissionResponse | null;
  finalScore: number | null;
}

private readonly storageKey = 'geoguesser.game-state';

private saveState(): void {
  sessionStorage.setItem(
    this.storageKey,
    JSON.stringify({
      round: this.game.round(),
      phase: this.phase(),
      result: this.result(),
      finalScore: this.finalScore(),
    } satisfies SavedGameState),
  );
}
```

In `ngOnInit()`, restore this state before calling `startGame()`. Call `saveState()` after:

- a guess changes the phase to `result`;
- loading the next round;
- loading the final score;
- successfully starting Play Again.

